  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only the task-level search and approach actions, color observations, claim actions and receptions, pickup and drop actions and outcomes, and matching delivery publications required for one-box delivery. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because the fixed collision_avoidance specification already constrains the selected task-level motion actions against obstacle observations.",
    "transition_design": "object_search repeatedly enables search_object and branches to a color-specific claim-attempt state only after the corresponding object-visible observation. Each claim-attempt state abandons the candidate on its matching received-claim or not-visible observation. A successful claim immediately enables repeated approach_object; loss of visibility returns to color-specific object search, and pickup is enabled only after the matching object-reached observation. Pickup confirmation starts search for only the matching zone, while pickup failure retries the claimed object. Zone visibility enables repeated approach_zone, loss of visibility returns to zone search, and drop_object is enabled only after the matching zone-reached observation. Delivery failure retries the matching zone, while confirmation is followed by the matching publication and delivery_complete. No delivery actions leave delivery_complete, enforcing at most one delivered box per robot.",
